References: <3BZQf3IgvoY.UnKWCtCHQdkJ@mirt-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/3BZQf3IgvoY/m/0-cz_a5gnXQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Yutaro,

Yes, slope parameters can be negative, and in bifactor models this often happens in the specific factors. It's nothing to worry about since slopes are 'partial regression coefficients', so the results are in no way paradoxical. Cheers.

Phil

