These were added to the dev version a while back, but will also require the dev version of mirt.

>
> With the "KL" criterion, all the items are admnistered to reach the default 0.3 threshold for the SEM (which is not reached for all the dimensions), is there a reasonable standard in the literature for the SEM threshold ?

Not that I'm aware of, but I'm fairly new to the literature.

>
> Hung & al (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23749433) proposes the value 3.3 as threshold but it seems weird given the SE take the values 1 at the first step of theta estimation....

That has to be a typo. A standard error of 3.3 would converge instantly in any Bayesian estimate, an almost immediately in ML estimation (you would know a theta value of CI = theta +- 1.96 * 3.3 = [?,?], that's massive and pointless). Maybe they mean 0.33?

Phil

